# Probe 37 (scripts/probe_pie_donut_options.py): the labels and legend options pie and donut were never probed for, the last two core chart types with none.
# Seen (bridge captures of both pages, then a real Home > Refresh + Ctrl+S): pie and donut behaved identically, and every candidate drew. The control (no objects) showed detail labels AND a legend at the RIGHT on both types, so their default differs from the area chart's bottom legend in probe 35. objects.labels.show = false removed the slice labels on both; show = true matched the control, since labels are on by default. objects.legend.position 'Top' moved the legend above the chart on both; 'Right' matched the control's default and so is indistinguishable there. objects.legend.show = false left no legend. P5 FAILED, which was the point of writing it: the object is called labels on these types, exactly as on the cartesian charts. The save rewrote NO visual.json at all — every candidate is still on disk byte for byte, with none of the $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 bump or auto filterConfig probe 35 saw on its active page — and changed only pages.json activePageName. All content invented.

######## blueprint: apply specs/ (six pies, six donuts)

